ogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b25\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">Thought: I need to use the PublicHolidayPublicHolidaysV3 tool to get the list of public holidays in Australia in 2023</title>\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">I&apos;m curious about the public holidays in Australia in 2023</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Assistant Can you fetch the list for me? Action: PublicHolidayPublicHolidaysV3 Action Input: {&quot;countryCode&quot;: &quot;AU&quot;, &quot;year&quot;: 2023} [Tool]: The output is too long. You need to use the &apos;retrievalDataFromFile&apos; function to retrieve the output from the file: ./tmp/retrieval_1692114481.txt</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b26\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">Labour Day -March 6th (observed in AU-WA)\\n4. Canberra Day -March 13th (observed in AU-ACT)\\n5. March Public Holiday -March 13th (observed in AU-SA)\\n6. Eight Hours Day -March 13th (observed in AU-TAS)\\n7. Labour Day -March 13th</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><surname>Assistant</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">Action: retrievalDataFromFile Action Input: {&quot;file_path&quot;: &quot;./tmp/retrieval_1692114481.txt&quot;, &quot;query&quot;: &quot;public holidays in Australia in 2023&quot;} [Tool]: {&quot;retrieved_info&quot;: &quot;Public Holidays in Australia in 2023:\\n1. New Year&apos;s Day -January 1st\\n2. Australia Day -January 26th\\n3</title>\n\t\t<title level=\"s\">observed in AU-VIC)\\n8. Good Friday</title>\n\t\t<meeting><address><addrLine>AU-ACT, AU-NSW, AU-NT, AU-QLD</addrLine></address></meeting>\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<date>April 7th\\n9. April 8th</date>\n\t\t\t<biblScope unit=\"page\">10</biblScope>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t\t<respStmt>\n\t\t\t<orgName>AU-SA ; AU-VIC</orgName>\n\t\t</respStmt>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Thought: I need to use the retrievalDataFromFile tool to retrieve the output from the file Holy Saturday (Easter Eve</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b27\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">Labour Day -May 1st (observed in AU-QLD)\\n15. Reconciliation Day -May 29th (observed in AU-ACT)\\n16. Western Australia Day -June 5th (observed in AU-WA)\\n17. King&apos;s Birthday -June 12th</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Easter</forename><surname>Sunday</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">- ; Au-Act</forename><surname>Au-Nsw</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Au-Vic</forename></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Au-Wa)\\n11</forename><forename type=\"middle\">Easter</forename><surname>Monday</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">Thought: The output from the file contains the list of public holidays in Australia in 2023. Response: The public holidays in Australia in 2023 are New Year&apos;s Day</title>\n\t\t<editor>\n\t\t\t<persName><surname>Au-Act</surname></persName>\n\t\t</editor>\n\t\t<editor>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Au-Nt</forename><surname>Au-Nsw</surname></persName>\n\t\t</editor>\n\t\t<editor>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Au-Sa</forename></persName>\n\t\t</editor>\n\t\t<editor>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Au-Tas</forename></persName>\n\t\t</editor>\n\t\t<meeting><address><addrLine>AU-ACT, AU-NSW, AU</addrLine></address></meeting>\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<publisher>Good Friday</publisher>\n\t\t\t<date>April 9th. April 10th\\n12. January 1st. January 26th. March 6th. March 13th. March 13th. April</date>\n\t\t\t<biblScope unit=\"volume\">18</biblScope>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t\t<respStmt>\n\t\t\t<orgName>AU-VIC</orgName>\n\t\t</respStmt>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Anzac Day -April 25th\\n13. May Day -May 1st (observed in AU-NT)\\n14 Picnic Day -August 7th (observed in AU-NT)\\n19 Labour Day -October 2nd -SA)\\n20. Christmas Day -December 25th\\n21. Boxing Day -December 26th Labour Day Eight Hours Day (March 13th Labour Day (March 13th</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b28\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Holy</forename><surname>Saturday</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">Easter Sunday</title>\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<date>April 8th. April</date>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Easter Eve</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b29\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">Labour Day (October 2nd), Christmas Day (December 25th), and Boxing Day (December 26th). Case for Real-world API: Currency Beacon [User]: I&apos;m a business owner and I need to invoice a client in Europe. Can you provide me with the current exchange rate from US dollars to Euros, and also the average rate for the July so I can set a fair price? Authentication information: api_key=*** [Assistant]: Thought: I need to get the current exchange rate and the average rate for July</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Easter</forename><surname>Monday</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<ptr target=\"https://currencybeacon.com/terms\" />\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">Western Australia Day</title>\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<date>April 10th. April 25th. May Day (May 1st. May 1st. May 29th. June 5th. June 12th. August 7th</date>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Anzac Day Reconciliation Day Labour Day Picnic Day King&apos;s Birthday Input: {&quot;api_key&quot;: &quot;***&quot;, &quot;base&quot;: &quot;USD&quot;, &quot;symbols&quot;: &quot;EUR&quot;} [Tool]: Status Code: 200. Response: {&quot;meta&quot;: {&quot;code&quot;: 200, &quot;disclaimer&quot;: &quot;Usage subject to terms }, &quot;response&quot;: {&quot;date&quot;: &quot;2023-08-15T16:46:58Z&quot;, &quot;base&quot;: &quot;USD&quot;, &quot;rates&quot;: {&quot;EUR&quot;: 0.91572671}}, &quot;date&quot;: &quot;2023-08-15T16:46:58Z&quot;, &quot;base&quot;: &quot;USD&quot;, &quot;rates&quot;: {&quot;EUR</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b30\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">91572671}}</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b31\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">Thought: I have the current exchange rate from US dollars to Euros</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><surname>Assistant</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<idno>]: Status Code: 200. Response: {&quot;meta&quot;: {&quot;code&quot;: 200</idno>\n\t\t<ptr target=\"https://currencybeacon.com/terms\" />\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">Action: historical_get Action Input: {&quot;api_key&quot;: &quot;***</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>&quot;, &quot;base&quot;: &quot;USD&quot;, &quot;date&quot;: &quot;2023-07-01&quot;, &quot;symbols&quot;: &quot;EUR&quot;} [Tool Usage subject to terms }, &quot;response&quot;: {&quot;date&quot;: &quot;2023-07-01&quot;, &quot;base&quot;: &quot;USD&quot;, &quot;rates&quot;: {&quot;EUR&quot;: 0.91706262}}, &quot;date&quot;: &quot;2023-07-01&quot;, &quot;base&quot;: &quot;USD&quot;, &quot;rates&quot;: {&quot;EUR&quot;: 0.91706262}} [Assistant]: Thought: I have the average rate for July. Response: The current exchange rate from US dollars to Euros is</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b32\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">Can you help me check the weather conditions for the major cities along the route, like Chicago, Denver, and Las Vegas? I&apos;d like to know if there will be any severe weather conditions that might affect my trip</title>\n\t\t<idno>2023-08-15 12:18</idno>\n\t\t<ptr target=\"https://cdn.worldweatheronline.com/images/wsymbols01_png_64/\" />\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">units&quot;: &quot;m&quot;, &quot;callback&quot;: &quot;weatherResponse&quot;} [Tool]: Status Code: 200. Response: weatherResponse({&quot;request&quot;: {&quot;type&quot;: &quot;City&quot;, &quot;query&quot;: &quot;Denver, United States of America</title>\n\t\t<meeting><address><addrLine>New York, Chicago, Denver, Las Vegas</addrLine></address></meeting>\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<date>July was 0.91706262</date>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Los Angeles next week Authentication information: access_key=*** [Assistant]: Thought: I need to get the weather conditions for the major cities along the route. Action: current_get Action Input: {&quot;access_key&quot;: &quot;*** Figure 15: Cases for real-world API: Currency Beacon. Case for Real-world API: apilayer weatherstack language&quot;: &quot;en&quot;, &quot;unit&quot;: &quot;m&quot;}, &quot;location&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;Denver&quot;, &quot;country&quot;: &quot;United States of America&quot;, &quot;region&quot;: &quot;New York&quot;, &quot;lat&quot;: &quot;42.213&quot;, &quot;lon&quot;: &quot;-74.570&quot;, &quot;timezone_id&quot;: &quot;America/New_York&quot;, &quot;localtime&quot; localtime_epoch&quot;: 1692101880, &quot;utc_offset&quot;: &quot;-4.0&quot;}, &quot;current&quot;: {&quot;observation_time&quot;: &quot;04:18 PM&quot;, &quot;temperature&quot;: 17, &quot;weather_code&quot;: 143, &quot;weather_icons wsymbol_0006_mist.png&quot;], &quot;weather_descriptions&quot;: [&quot;Mist&quot;], &quot;wind_speed&quot;: 4, &quot;wind_degree&quot;: 24, &quot;wind_dir&quot;: &quot;NNE&quot;, &quot;pressure&quot;: 1009, &quot;precip&quot;: 0, &quot;humidity&quot;: 96, &quot;cloudcover&quot;: 100, &quot;feelslike&quot;: 17, &quot;uv_index&quot;: 4, &quot;visibility&quot;: 0, &quot;is_day&quot;: &quot;yes&quot;}}) [Assistant]: Thought: The response from the current_get tool indicates that the weather in Denver is currently misty with a temperature of 17°C Action: current_get Action Input: {&quot;access_key&quot;: &quot;***&quot;, &quot;query&quot;: &quot;Chicago, United States of America&quot;, &quot;units&quot;: &quot;m&quot;, &quot;callback&quot;: &quot;weatherResponse&quot;} [Tool]: Status Code: 200. Response: ..</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b33\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><surname>Assistant</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">Thought: The response from the current_get tool indicates that the weather in Chicago is currently lightly raining with a temperature of 19°C. Action: current_get Action Input: {&quot;access_key&quot;: &quot;***&quot;, &quot;query&quot;: &quot;Las Vegas</title>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>United States of America&quot;, &quot;units&quot;: &quot;m&quot;, &quot;callback&quot;: &quot;weatherResponse&quot;} [Tool]: Status Code: 200. Response: ..</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b34\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Thought: The response from the current_get tool indicates that the weather in Las Vegas is currently sunny with a temperature of 34°C. Response: The weather conditions for the major cities along the route from New York to Los Angeles are as follows: Denver: currently misty with a temperature of 17°C, Chicago: currently lightly raining with a temperature of 19°C</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><surname>Assistant</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint/>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>and Las Vegas: currently sunny with a temperature of 34°C</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n\t\t\t\t</listBibl>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</back>\n\t</text>\n</TEI>\n","pdf_hash":"e404e8de67fcc281667cd79d633179b9965873d69e27ce3d27dc2d5fd900267f","tables":[{"table_id":"tab_0","section_path_id":"1~28","section_ordinal":38,"caption":"Table 1 :","coordinates":null,"cells":[{"row":0,"column":0,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"text":"statistics # of